---
title: Mashed potatoes
servings: 4
tags: [vegetarian, holiday]
time: 35 minutes
source: Perfect Mashed Potatoes by Elise Bauer, Simply Recipes, https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/perfect_mashed_potatoes/
---

Put the @Yukon Gold potatoes{1.5%lb}(peeled and quartered lengthwise) in a
#medium saucepan{} and cover with cold water by at least an inch. Add
@salt{1/2%tsp}.

Bring to a boil over high heat, then turn down to a simmer, cover, and cook
~{15%minutes} to 20 minutes, until a fork goes through easily.

Meanwhile, warm the @heavy cream{4%tbsp} and @unsalted butter{2%tbsp} together
until the butter melts.

Drain the potatoes and put them, still steaming, in a #large bowl{}. Pour over
the cream and butter, add another @salt{1/2%tsp}, and mash with a
#potato masher{}.

Stir in the @whole milk{1%tbsp}(or more), a tablespoon at a time, with a wooden
spoon until just smooth. Season with salt and @black pepper{}.

> Stop stirring as soon as they are smooth; overworked potatoes turn gluey.
